An authoritative Daniel approval response names the evidence/design revision and any conditions. The gate remains blocked on rejection or clarification. Implementation agents MUST NOT close this Bead; currentization and downstream dependencies cannot become ready through unrelated closure.

## Acceptance Criteria
A complete non-authoritative Gate #2 candidate is assembled across all approved maintained surfaces. Its packet contains:

- OpenSpec validation and requirement-graph equivalence evidence;
- delegated Quint structural-equivalence evidence covering state space, transitions, guards, invariants, outcomes, release, parameters, and bounds;
- reviewed-state migration evidence preserving fingerprints, outcomes, reasons, and old-to-new correspondence;
- focused Rust, trace, compatibility, and documentation verification;
- a stale retired-terminology scan across maintained current surfaces;
- a classification distinguishing legitimate retained narrow meanings from actual stale migration misses;
- the exact proposed shared-Bead edits from `.7`;
- confirmation that no real canonical/current-authority cutover or shared-Bead vocabulary migration has occurred.

The packet also preserves explicit non-claims and is sufficient for Daniel Gate #2 review. Any unowned stale primary name, orphaned ID, unexplained fingerprint churn, semantic distinction loss, unresolved authority conflict, or missing candidate surface keeps this Bead open with the exact repair required. Completion makes only `.9` ready; `.10` cannot become ready until Daniel closes `.9`.
